      "benchmark": "gru",
      "title": "Half output is distinct from half arithmetic",
      "observation": "The selected GRU cell computes sigmoid/tanh gates and intermediate combinations with Float32 arithmetic, projects outputs and five saved-state planes into Float16, and widens those arrays for the artifact outside the timer. Gate-affine inputs are already supplied: this does not time their matrix multiplications, a full recurrent network, or training. GPP separately uses Float64 split-complex reductions, illustrating why scientific stage and source arithmetic need distinct fields.",
